#reference 1
@Author MacKerell et al.
@Date 1998
A. D. MacKerell Jr., D. Bashford, M. Bellott, R. L. Dunbrack Jr., J. D. Evanseck, M. J. Field, S. Fischer, J. Gao, H. Guo, S. Ha, D. Joseph-McCarthy, L. Kuchnir, K. Kuczera, F. T. K. Lau, C. Mattos, S. Michnick, T. Ngo, D. T. Nguyen, B. Prodhom, W. E. Reiher III, B. Roux, M. Schlenkrich, J. C. Smith, R. Stote, J. Straub, M. Watanabe, J. Wiorkiewicz-Kuczera, D. Yin and M. Karplus, "All-Atom Empirical Potential for Molecular Modeling and Dynamics Studies of Proteins", J. Phys. Chem. B 102, 3586-3616 (1998), https://doi.org/10.1021/jp973084f. Equation 1 (the functional form) and the Appendix of the Supporting Information (the parameters).

#reference 2
@Author MacKerell laboratory toppar distribution
@Date 2024
Converted from the CHARMM22 all-hydrogen protein parameter and topology files par_all22_prot.prm and top_all22_prot.rtf (December 2003 revision, CMAP block omitted) of the July 2024 CHARMM force-field distribution of the MacKerell laboratory, https://mackerell.umaryland.edu/charmm_ff.shtml (a public download that carries no license text). The parameter values are those published in reference 1 (the Appendix of its Supporting Information) and references 3 and 4; this file is a new expression of them in the SEAMM format, generated for xnn, and copies no file text beyond the one-line atom-type descriptions. Residues are the topology file's RESI entries with their impropers; the terminal and patched forms (NTER, GLYP, PROP, CTER, CT2, DISU, ASPP, GLUP, LSN) were generated by applying the file's patches, and the ACE / CT3 capping groups are fragments of their own. The residue SMARTS are generated from the topology connectivity with element, degree and hydrogen-count constraints and atom maps in topology order; the per-type SMARTS templates for small molecules were written for xnn after the atom-type descriptions of the files.

#reference 3
@Author Jorgensen et al.
@Date 1983
W. L. Jorgensen, J. Chandrasekhar, J. D. Madura, R. W. Impey and M. L. Klein, "Comparison of simple potential functions for simulating liquid water", J. Chem. Phys. 79, 926-935 (1983), https://doi.org/10.1063/1.445869 (TIP3P, in the CHARMM modification of toppar_water_ions.str).

#reference 4
@Author Beglov and Roux; Stote and Karplus
@Date 1994; 1995
D. Beglov and B. Roux, "Finite representation of an infinite bulk system: solvent boundary potential for computer simulations", J. Chem. Phys. 100, 9050-9063 (1994), https://doi.org/10.1063/1.466711 (ions, as revised in toppar_water_ions.str, with the ion-carboxylate pair overrides it carries); R. H. Stote and M. Karplus, "Zinc binding in proteins and solution: a simple but accurate nonbonded representation", Proteins 23, 12-31 (1995), https://doi.org/10.1002/prot.340230104 (zinc).

#end
